 more or less the same for most  the movie but the best change was the  ending  Mowgli's entire life was in the jungle  the  the Panther and Baloo are his family in  the live-action movie he defeats Shere  Khan and he decides to stay with his  family in the jungle it got us right in  the fields we loved all the changes in  this version UT and the Beast Disney  remade a bunch of the classic era films  before diving into the Disney  Renaissance but in 2017 they decided to  remake some of the more modern animated  movies they started with Beauty and the  Beast the 1991 version was a classic  that was unhappy in her village Belle  and her dad are total outcasts she saves  her father by sacrificing herself to the  Beast to a nearby enchanted castle all  of the castles staff have been turned  into household objects the music is  amazing and Belle is a much more  powerful heroine than the princesses who  came before her but it always left us  with a lot of questions why is it winter  in the nearby castle why do none of the  villagers know that a prince lives a few  hours away the 2017 version answered all  of these questions The Enchantress who  cursed the prince made the villagers  forget all about the castle and she also  cast a spell that caused the kingdom to  be stuck in a state of perpetual winter  but one of the best changes in the  live-action remake was Belle's  personality she's a lot more of a  go-getter she still loves books but  she's also an inventor  she even invents a laundry machine at  the beginning of the film she also takes  her fate into her own hands and tries to  escape right away it's pretty clear that  after the first night she is no longer a  prisoner  we loved Belle's modern upgrade  Christopher Robin our next live-action  Disney movie isn't a remake of just one  film but it does give us a whole new  look into the world of Winnie the Pooh  Disney has made a lot of Winnie the Pooh  stories there have been several movies  and TV shows some were really popular  like the Tigger movie and they are all  little different but they all featured  the same lovable stuffed animals who  live in the 100 Acre Wood these  characters are based on a real boy named  Christopher Robin and his lively stuffed  animals in 2018 Disney released  Christopher Robin we get to see  Christopher Robin and his pals as kids  but the boys forced to grow up  to fast as an adult he is not really  happy with his life but then his  childhood stuffed bear shows up and he  can talk Christopher reunites with his  old toys he masters what it means to be  a kid again he learns what is really  important in life like his family  Christopher turns his life around with  the help of Pooh in the gang it's  adorable and it will hit kids and adults  right in the fields we just love that  Disney decided to show us a grown-up  Christopher Robin Dumbo the original  Dumbo is the fourth Disney animated  movie to ever be created it was released  in 1941 the movie is about a circus  elephants names Dumbo who has huge ears  and he can fly he gets separated from  his mom as a baby but with the help of a  mouse he becomes a star eventually he is  reunited with his mom but they get their  own act it's a total tearjerker but it's  a classic nonetheless Dumbo was remade  into a live-action film and released in  2019 this movie is still pretty new so  if you haven't seen it skip ahead  because spoilers are coming up quick  anyway the live-action film is very  different from the original but these  changes were all super necessary in the  last few decades circuses have been  criticized for animal cruelty and the  movie didn't shy away from the truth one  of the best changes was the addition of  two new characters Millie and Joe who  happened to be the children of Dumbo's  caretaker they go out of their way to  help Dumbo reunite with his mom but the  best change is the end Dumbo and his  mother are reunited and they get to live  with the other elephants in the wild we  love this ending so much Aladdin it  looks like 2019 is the year of  live-action Disney remakes and we aren't  complaining the original aladdin came  out in 1992 it's about an orphan boy who  finds a magic lamp he gets a genie who  helps him become a rich prince this  helps him win the hand of Princess  Jasmine  I choose you he defeats the evil Jafar  and lives happily ever after the new  movie looks pretty similar to the  original but the real sets and costumes  are amazing we're pretty bummed that  Robin Williams is no longer around to  play the genie  but for confident that Will Smith will  do a great job there's one major change  we are really excited about and it has  to do with Princess Jasmine she's not  just a girl who sits alone waiting to be  married off she is a political force who  stands up to her dad the Sultan and she  has a handmaiden who is also her best  friend they support each other no matter  what we're so happy to see that Princess  Jasmine has a human friend in the  live-action movie no offence Raja The  Lion King okay we're using the term  live-action a little loosely here but a  brand-new CGI version of The Lion King  is coming out in July of 2019 and we  cannot wait the original version of The  Lion King is one of the most successful  movies of all time the 1994 movie was  about Simba a young lion cub he is the  son of the King Mufasa  but Mufasa is betrayed by his evil  brother scar which results in him losing  his life young Simba is forced to run  away into the jungle he is raised by  Timon and Pumbaa his childhood friends  Nala finds him and brings him home he  defeats scar and becomes king it's an  epic movie with an amazing soundtrack  the movie looks like it will have pretty  much the same plot but we are so excited  about some of the new cast members Seth  Rogen is playing  Pumbaa he will be perfect for the goofy  warthog Donald Glover is voicing Simba  and Elton John and Tim Rice are writing  a brand new song for the movie we cannot 